		{"id":"image-century","type":"text","text":"## II. LAST HUNDRED YEARS\n\nTHE CLOSURE\n\nA new fear or event changes the state.","x":-450,"y":-540,"width":800,"height":380,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"century-open","type":"text","text":"## THE CENTURY IS A CAUSAL CAMP\n\nThe Ossuary closure is fixed at **70 years ago**. The storm's timing, the route-collapse sequence, and the Hearthborn failure belong to the same historical turn, though their order is not yet known. A thread may straddle eras when causes and consequences overlap.","x":-450,"y":880,"width":790,"height":240,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"scale-war","type":"file","file":"World/Cultures/Ossuary States/Scale, War, and Catastrophe.md","x":-1450,"y":570,"width":370,"height":260,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"distant-open","type":"text","text":"## CHRONOLOGY LOST TO TIME\n\n- Travelers arrive and depart\n- Earlier realm crisis\n- Great cultivation disasters\n- Walking Haven construction\n\nTheir exact dates are unknown; their relationship to the present keeps them in the distant past.","x":-1030,"y":570,"width":370,"height":260,"color":"6"},
